          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Edvard Grieg</strong><br>\nEdvard Grieg was born on June 15, 1843, in Bergen, Norway, into a musical family. His mother, Gesine, was his first piano teacher and laid the foundation for his musical education. Recognizing his talent at a young age, Grieg was sent to study at the Leipzig Conservatory in Germany when he was just 15 years old. His studies there exposed him to the works of the masters, but he also suffered from a severe lung disease during this time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Grieg's Nationalistic Influence</strong><br>\nGrieg's music was deeply influenced by Norwegian folk culture. After finishing his studies in Leipzig, he returned to Norway, where he sought to develop a national form of music. Grieg was inspired by the Norwegian landscape, folk tunes, and dances. He believed that the music of Norway could be elevated to new artistic heights and worked to incorporate these elements into his compositions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Career Highlights</strong><br>\nGrieg achieved early success as a composer with his Piano Concerto in A minor, which premiered in Copenhagen in 1868. This concerto became one of his most famous works and is still popular today. He continued to compose music that was characteristic of Norway, gaining acclaim across Europe. His compositions include a range of works from piano solo pieces to orchestral works.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
