          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Years and Death</strong><br>\nGrieg's later years were marked by a decline in health but also by recognition of his contributions to music. He was honored by music societies and royals across Europe. Grieg died on September 4, 1907, leaving behind a legacy that has influenced many generations of composers and musicians.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Grieg's Legacy</strong><br>\nGrieg's impact on music extends beyond Norway and his compositions are part of the standard classical repertoire worldwide. His ability to combine elements of Norwegian folk music with classical traditions created a distinctive sound that has inspired countless other musicians. His legacy is celebrated annually at the Bergen International Festival.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Educational Influence</strong><br>\nGrieg's life and works are not only important for their artistic value but also for their educational importance. His compositions are often used to teach musical concepts and history, and his life story is a testament to the power of cultural influence on art. Grieg's dedication to music education has made him a national icon in Norway and an important figure in musical education around the world.</p>\n"
              },
